---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

// The widget posts its height; this listener sizes the frame to fit. It only trusts messages from
// our own origin, and only from a frame that is actually one of ours on the host page.
const resizer = `<script>addEventListener("message",function(e){if(e.origin!=="${SITE.url}"||!e.data||e.data.type!=="ctc:height")return;var h=Math.min(Math.max(+e.data.height||0,300),2000);document.querySelectorAll("iframe[data-ctc-embed]").forEach(function(f){if(f.contentWindow===e.source)f.style.height=h+"px"})})</script>`;
const snippet = `<iframe src="${SITE.url}/embed" title="CTC to in-hand salary calculator" width="100%" height="900" style="border:0;max-width:560px" loading="lazy" data-ctc-embed></iframe>
${resizer}
<p><a href="${SITE.url}/">CTC to in-hand salary calculator</a> by ${SITE.name}</p>`;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Embed the calculator on your site"
  description={`Add a free CTC to in-hand salary calculator to your blog or HR site. One snippet, both tax regimes, ${SITE.shortYearLabel} rates, kept up to date for you.`}
  updated="2026-10-09"
>
  <p>
    If you write about salaries, offers or payroll, you can put a working CTC calculator on your own
    page. It uses the same engine as this site, compares both tax regimes and applies your reader's
    state professional tax. When the law changes, the embedded calculator updates on its own.
  </p>

  <h2>The snippet</h2>
  <p>Paste this where you want the calculator to appear:</p>
  <pre
    class="overflow-x-auto rounded-sm bg-sunken p-4 text-xs leading-5 text-ink"
    tabindex="0"
    aria-label="Embed snippet"
  ><code id="embed-snippet">{snippet}</code></pre>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-copy-snippet>
      Copy the snippet
    </button>
  </p>
  <p>
    The short script lets the frame grow and shrink to fit the calculator, so nothing is cut off on
    a phone. If your site does not allow scripts, leave it out and set the height yourself: 900
    suits most columns, about 1,000 one narrower than 360px. Add <code>?theme=dark</code> or{' '}
    <code>?theme=light</code> to the address to fix the colour scheme; otherwise it follows your
    reader's system setting.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. Please keep the credit line under the calculator: it is how people find the full
    breakdown, and how we keep this free. Everything is worked out in your reader's browser: the
    calculator sets no cookies and sends none of the figures anywhere. The only thing recorded is an
    anonymous page view in our Cloudflare Web Analytics totals.
  </p>

  <h2>Preview</h2>
  <iframe
    src="/embed"
    title="CTC to in-hand salary calculator"
    width="100%"
    height="900"
    style="border:0;max-width:560px"
    loading="lazy"
    data-ctc-embed
  ></iframe>
</DocLayout>

<script>
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-snippet]');
  const code = document.getElementById('embed-snippet');
  // The preview sizes itself the same way the snippet does, from this site's own origin.
  window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {
    if (event.origin !== window.location.origin || event.data?.type !== 'ctc:height') return;
    const height = Math.min(Math.max(Number(event.data.height) || 0, 300), 2000);
    for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLIFrameElement>('iframe[data-ctc-embed]')) {
      if (frame.contentWindow === event.source) frame.style.height = `${height}px`;
    }
  });

  button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const text = code?.textContent ?? '';
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
      button.textContent = 'Copied';
    } catch {
      window.prompt('Copy the snippet', text);
    }
    window.setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = 'Copy the snippet'), 2000);
  });
</script>
